<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilgit</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gilgit is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgit-baltistan">Gilgit-Baltistan</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, on the Gilgit river near its junction with the Hunza. A stop on routes linking South and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, it is known for the Gilgit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, Buddhist texts of the 5th to 7th centuries found nearby. It came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dogras">Dogra</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> in the 19th century, and its 1947 uprising brought the region under Pakistani control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gilgit.jpg" alt="Gilgit" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fehd.raza @fehd.raza · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gilgit_City_a_View_from_Gilgit_serena_hotel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
